#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Answer questions in @PCoinPCNChat, and file everything worth a human's time.

    pcoin-group-answer                 one pass; run it from a timer
    pcoin-group-answer --dry-run       decide and print, post nothing, file nothing
    pcoin-group-answer --status        what it knows, touching nothing

IT DOES NOT POLL TELEGRAM. `getUpdates` is exclusive and `pcoin-group-watch` is
this estate's only permitted consumer of it -- two consumers steal each other's
updates and each sees half a conversation, which was live on two hosts until
2026-09-13. So the watcher writes every group message to a spool file and this
reads that. The relay stays the load-bearing path: if this script is broken,
stopped or wrong, the operator still gets every message.

IT SHIPS SWITCHED OFF. ANSWER_MODE defaults to `shadow`: it decides, drafts, and
files the draft for review, but posts nothing. Nothing it writes reaches the
group until somebody has read a batch of drafts and set ANSWER_MODE=live. A bot
that starts talking to real users on the strength of its author's confidence is
how a project ends up apologising in public.

WHAT IT WILL NOT SAY. The prompt tells it not to discuss infrastructure or quote
live rates. That is necessary and not sufficient -- a prompt is a request, not a
mechanism -- so every draft is also checked here, and one that mentions a host,
a path, a credential-shaped string or a PCN rate is held back for a human no
matter how confident the model was.
"""
